              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              both by their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform"} Fourier transform
              (inserting the Fourier expression of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delta+distribution"} delta distribution
              from
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Dirac+distribution#FourierTransformOfDeltaDistribution"} this example
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+derivative"} partial derivative
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mfrac
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi a
                    %mfrac
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi^{a b} \frac{\partial}{\partial\phi^a}{\frac{\partial}{\phi^b}}
              turns into the product with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %msup
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \pi^{i j} k_i k_j
              (
              %a{:href => "Fourier+transform#BasicPropertiesOfFourierTransformOverCartesianSpaces"}> this prop.
              ). Then we identified again the Fourier-expansion of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delta+distribution"} delta distribution
              and finally we applied the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/change+of+integration+variables"} change of integration variables
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi ℏ
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = \tfrac{1}{\hbar}\omega \cdot z
              and then evaluated the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delta+distribution"} delta distribution
          %p
            Next we express this as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+convolution+product"} groupoid convolution product
            of polarized sections of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+groupoid"} symplectic groupoid
          #SymplecticGroupoidOfSymplecticVectorSpace.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+groupoid"} symplectic groupoid
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+vector+space"} symplectic vector space
            %p
              Assume that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
              is the inverse of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+form"} symplectic form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{2n}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi n
                            %mo ×
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi n
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi pr
